# Version Release Workflow

When asked to create a new release item, read the **latest** `## Released on:` block in `CHANGELOG.md` and use its **Custom version** table and **Release note** as the source of truth.

## Input: Custom version table

| Platform | Build Number | Test Build Number | Version |
| -------- | ------------ | ----------------- | ------- |
| Android  | {A_BN}       | {T}               | {A_VER} |
| iOS      | {I_BN}       | {T}               | {I_VER} |

## Step 1 — Generate the Git note release block

Append under the latest release's `### Release note:` section:

### Git note release:

#### Command for copilot

`[Builded] Version {A_VER} - {A_BN} / {I_VER} - {I_BN} _ {release_note} `

#### Brief for Store's new update:

_ {EN line 1 — expand the release note into a user-facing sentence}
_ {EN line 2 — optional second point}
_ {VI line 1 — Vietnamese translation of EN line 1}
_ {VI line 2 — Vietnamese translation of EN line 2}

#### Flutter build for Android for Testing (Development)

`npm run flutterfire_setup_dev && flutter build appbundle --build-name={A_VER}.{T} --build-number={A_BN} --release --dart-define=APP_ENVIRONMENT=DEVELOPMENT`

#### Flutter build for iOS for Testing (Development)

`npm run flutterfire_setup_dev && flutter build ios --build-name={I_VER} --build-number={I_BN}.{T} --release --dart-define=APP_ENVIRONMENT=DEVELOPMENT`

#### Flutter build for Android

`npm run flutterfire_setup && flutter build appbundle --build-name={A_VER} --build-number={A_BN} --release --dart-define=APP_ENVIRONMENT=PRODUCTION`

#### Flutter build for iOS

`npm run flutterfire_setup && flutter build ios --build-name={I_VER} --build-number={I_BN} --release --dart-define=APP_ENVIRONMENT=PRODUCTION`

#### Fastlane deploy for Testing (Development)

`(cd android && bundle exec fastlane deploy_staging build_name:{A_VER}.{T} build_number:{A_BN})`

`(cd ios && bundle exec fastlane deploy_staging build_name:{I_VER} build_number:{I_BN}.{T})`

#### Fastlane deploy for Production

`(cd android && bundle exec fastlane deploy_production build_name:{A_VER} build_number:{A_BN} update_screenshots:false)`

`(cd ios && bundle exec fastlane deploy_production build_name:{I_VER} build_number:{I_BN} submit:true update_screenshots:false)`

Rules for these blocks:
- Keep the `flutter build …` lines exactly in this shape — the Fastlane lanes
  parse the latest block's `flutter build appbundle|ios … APP_ENVIRONMENT=…`
  lines for the default version, and its **Brief for Store's new update**
  bullets for the store "What's new" (lines with Vietnamese letters → `vi`,
  the rest → `en-US`). Brief lines must start with `_ `.
- The Fastlane lines use the same numbers as the matching `flutter build` line
  (Development ↔ `deploy_staging`, Production ↔ `deploy_production`).
- The iOS production line always has `submit:true`: an iOS production
  deploy always submits the version for App Review.
- Both production lines carry `update_screenshots:` — `false` by default
  (store screenshots untouched). Write `true` only when the user asks to
  update the screenshots with this release; then the lanes upload the sets
  from `android/fastlane/metadata/android/<locale>/images/` and
  `ios/fastlane/screenshots/<locale>/` (made by `tool/screenshots/capture.sh`
  — re-capture first if the UI changed).

## Step 2 — Update `.github/config/version-config.json`

Overwrite the file with values derived from the same table. `releaseNotes` must match the Brief above.

```json
{
"android": {
  "dev":  { "versionName": "{A_VER}.{T}", "versionCode": {A_BN}, "releaseNotes": { "en-US": "...", "vi-VN": "..." } },
  "prod": { "versionName": "{A_VER}",     "versionCode": {A_BN}, "releaseNotes": { "en-US": "...", "vi-VN": "..." } }
},
"ios": {
  "dev":  { "versionName": "{I_VER}", "buildNumber": "{I_BN}.{T}", "releaseNotes": { "en-US": "...", "vi-VN": "..." } },
  "prod": { "versionName": "{I_VER}", "buildNumber": "{I_BN}",     "releaseNotes": { "en-US": "...", "vi-VN": "..." } }
},
"metadata": { "lastUpdated": "{Released on date as ISO 8601}", "updatedBy": "CI/CD Pipeline" }
}
```

## Step 3 — Git add and commit

Stage all changed files and commit using the Command for copilot message:

```bash
git add -A && git commit -m "[Builded] Version {A_VER} - {A_BN} / {I_VER} - {I_BN} _ {release_note}"
```

## Step 4 — Deploy with Fastlane (only when asked to deploy / publish)

The lanes, options and checks are one contract shared by all four BOM apps —
see `.agents/rules/fastlane-deployment.mdc`. A change to it is made in all four
repos together.

Never upload as part of creating a release item: deploying publishes to the
stores. Do it only when the user explicitly asks to deploy or publish. Details:
`docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`; keys: `.env.fastlane` (`docs/STORE_KEYS_SETUP.md`).

1. **Check keys and signing** (uploads nothing):
   ```bash
   (cd android && bundle exec fastlane check_env)
   (cd ios && bundle exec fastlane check_env)
   ```
2. **Store preflight** (builds nothing): can each store take this version?
   ```bash
   (cd android && bundle exec fastlane check_release build_name:{A_VER} build_number:{A_BN})
   (cd ios && bundle exec fastlane check_release build_name:{I_VER} build_number:{I_BN})
   ```
   If it fails, stop and report its reason (e.g. the version code is already
   used, or another iOS version is still in review) — don't change the numbers
   on your own. The deploy lanes run the same check before building.
3. **Dry run on Play** (builds, then Play validates the whole upload and
   discards it):
   ```bash
   (cd android && bundle exec fastlane deploy_production build_name:{A_VER} build_number:{A_BN} validate_only:true)
   ```
4. **Deploy** — the commands from the release block's **Fastlane deploy for
   Production** (or **…for Testing** for the internal track / TestFlight).
   Each lane does what the matching `flutter build` line does and uploads:
   - bundles the real app config (`env` for production, `env_dev` for
     staging) as `.env` for the build, then restores `.env`;
   - runs `npm run flutterfire_setup` / `flutterfire_setup_dev` itself — don't
     run it separately;
   - uploads the store "What's new" from the block's Brief (Play `en-US`/`vi`,
     TestFlight `en-US`, App Store `en-US`/`vi`).
   - iOS production is **always** run with `submit:true`: it submits the
     version for App Review after the upload (waiting for Apple to process
     the build). Never drop it or pass `submit:false`. If a submission fails
     after the upload succeeded, retry just the submission with
     `(cd ios && bundle exec fastlane submit_review build_name:{I_VER} build_number:{I_BN})`.
     After approval the release is manual unless `auto_release:true`.
   Options: `update_screenshots:true` (also replace the store screenshots —
   only when asked; the lane checks every locale has a set before building),
   `release_status:draft` (Play: upload without rolling out),
   `skip_flutterfire:true` (reuse the current Firebase config).
5. **Report** what was uploaded (platform, track, version, build number) and
   anything left to do by hand (e.g. releasing the iOS version after approval).
